Not from Solaris: OpenIndiana-only.

gdm hands the console tty to PAM (PAM_TTY) in set_up_for_current_vt(),
which it only calls when logind says "seat0" has VTs.  Without systemd
that is never the case.  Solaris' pam_unix_session accepts a session
without PAM_TTY; illumos' refuses it ("Can not make/remove entry for
session"), and the greeter session then never starts (gdm: "Session never
registered, failing").  Without systemd, set PAM_TTY (and XDISPLAY,
XAUTHDATA) from ConsoleKit's display device for every reused-VT session.

--- a/daemon/gdm-session-worker.c
+++ b/daemon/gdm-session-worker.c
@@ -2862,6 +2862,15 @@
         g_assert (worker->state == GDM_SESSION_WORKER_STATE_ACCOUNT_DETAILS_SAVED);
         g_assert (geteuid () == 0);
 
+#ifndef WITH_SYSTEMD
+        /* illumos: no logind to report VTs on "seat0"; the display device
+         * comes from ConsoleKit, and pam_unix_session needs it as PAM_TTY. */
+        if (worker->display_mode == GDM_SESSION_DISPLAY_MODE_REUSE_VT &&
+            !set_up_for_current_vt (worker, error)) {
+                return FALSE;
+        }
+#endif
+
         if (g_strcmp0 (worker->display_seat_id, "seat0") == 0 && worker->seat0_has_vts) {
                 switch (worker->display_mode) {
                 case GDM_SESSION_DISPLAY_MODE_REUSE_VT:
